Bugs seen on the live Modal site (driven with headless Chrome after the last deploy):
1. Mid-replay the web app got `GET /sessions/<id>/state?upto_seq=46 -> 404 {"detail":"unknown session"}` and ~24 other
   404s. `modal container list` shows TWO containers for app mmc: sessions live in one container's memory/volume view,
   and requests landing on the other container 404. Fix in modal_app.py: serve from a single container that handles
   concurrent requests (Modal 1.6.3: `max_containers=1` on @app.function plus `@modal.concurrent(max_inputs=...)`),
   keep one warm (`min_containers=1`, `scaledown_window` reasonable) for the judging period, and make a session/report
   lookup miss fall back to reading the volume (volume.reload()) before 404. Extend the offline stub test to assert
   these settings.
2. Report tab auto-opens report id bb5539d4... but `GET /reports/<id>.json -> 404 unknown report`: replaying a bundle
   restores the report_built event but not the report file it names. On replay, rebuild the report deterministically
   from the replayed state into that same id (Wonder review reused from the event, $0), or have the web call the
   report-build route which reuses it; the report must load in one click. Test with the vacuum-leak bundle.
3. modal_app.seed_fixtures copies a bundle only if the file doesn't exist on the volume, so updated bundles never reach
   the live site. Copy when the sha256 differs. Test it.
4. Number formatting in human labels: "Fuel trims: +18% at idle, +4.244416662221763% at 2,500 rpm". Round percentages
   to 1 decimal, volts to 2, everything human-facing.
5. The next-test column is very long: collapse each card's safety checklist and expected outcomes by default
   (expand on click; the checklist still has to be completed before a live run, unchanged).
Run the backend suite (< 3 min), make_demo_bundle.py --check, replay_check and the web build until green. Do not commit.
Foreground only. Finish with files changed and test counts.
